.\" jailops-backupd.8, installed as /usr/local/share/man/man8/jailops-backupd.8
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt JAILOPS-BACKUPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailops-backupd
.Nd the JailOps backup node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file | Fl -config Ar file
.Op Fl -json
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Ar command
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the backup node of JailOps: a server that stores the encrypted,
deduplicated backups of jails on a directory or an S3 bucket, with its control
plane in PostgreSQL.
It is keyless: it holds no key and never decrypts anything.
Backup hosts connect to one TLS listener (default port 39111) with a client
certificate whose fingerprint was enrolled; the management API and, when
enabled, the web console are served on the same port.
Administration happens through a unix socket that only root may use.
.Pp
The options may come before or after the command:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
The configuration file (YAML; unknown keys are an error).
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/backupd.yaml ,
or the value of
.Ev JAILOPS_BACKUPD_CONFIG .
.It Fl -json
Print raw JSON answers instead of text.
.It Fl -help , Fl -version
Print the usage, or the version, and exit.
.El
.Pp
The daemon:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm serve Op Fl -adopt
Run the node: the host listener, the admin socket, the management API and the
console.
.Fl -adopt
takes over a repository owned by another node that is gone for good.
.It Xo
.Cm init
.Op Fl -admin Ar name
.Op Fl -password-file Ar file | Fl -password-prompt
.Op Fl -key-domain Ar id
.Xc
Create the repository, probe the datastore, migrate the database, create the
server certificate (self-signed, when the files are missing) and print its
fingerprint, which the hosts pin.
With
.Fl -admin
the first administrator is created; the password comes from the file, from a
prompt on the terminal, or from standard input.
A second
.Cm init
reports the existing repository and its owner and exits 0.
.It Cm check-config
Load the configuration, read the database secret file (and the S3
credentials), and look for the TLS files; the network and the datastore are
not touched.
.It Cm version
Print the version and the database schema version.
.El
.Pp
Administration, through the admin socket of the running daemon:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
The repository status.
.It Cm gc Oo Fl -grace Ar duration Oc Op Fl -dry-run
Garbage collection.
The grace period defaults to the configuration and is at least 12 hours.
.It Cm verify Oo Cm all | new | stale Oc Op Fl -no-quarantine
Keyless verification of the chunks (default
.Cm new ) .
Corrupt chunks are moved aside unless
.Fl -no-quarantine
is given.
.It Cm retention Op Fl -dry-run
Apply the retention policies.
.It Cm maintenance Op Cm online | read-only | offline
Show or set the maintenance mode.
.It Cm protect Ar group snapshot , Cm unprotect Ar group snapshot
Protect a snapshot from deletion and retention, or stop protecting it.
.It Cm delete request Ar group snapshot Op Fl -delay Ar duration
.It Cm delete cancel Ar group snapshot
.It Cm delete execute Ar group snapshot
Request the deletion of a snapshot, cancel the request, or execute it once the
delay (default from the configuration) has passed.
.It Cm quarantine list
List the chunks verification moved aside.
.It Cm reconcile
Rebuild the snapshot index from the repository.
.It Cm jobs Op Ar id
Recent jobs, or one job with its result.
.El
.Pp
The database, directly:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm hosts enroll Ar name
.Pq Fl -fingerprint Ar fp | Fl -cert Ar file
.Op Fl -scopes Ar list
.Op Fl -note Ar text
.Xc
Enroll a backup host by the SHA-256 fingerprint of its certificate.
The scopes are
.Cm backup-push ,
.Cm backup-pull
and
.Cm restore
(default
.Cm backup-push,backup-pull ) ;
administration is never a host scope.
.It Cm hosts list , Cm hosts revoke Ar name
List the hosts, or revoke one: its open sessions are aborted and the daemon
stops accepting it within seconds.
.It Xo
.Cm users add Ar name role
.Op Fl -password-file Ar file | Fl -password-prompt
.Xc
.It Cm users list , Cm users delete Ar name
The users of the management API and console; the role is
.Cm readonly ,
.Cm backup-admin
or
.Cm admin .
.El
.Pp
.Cm completion Cm bash | zsh | fish
prints a completion script for the shell; the package installs them under
.Pa /usr/local/share .
.Sh RC.CONF
The rc.d script
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jailops_backupd
runs
.Cm serve
under
.Xr daemon 8
as the user
.Sy jailops-backup
and sends its output to syslog with the tag
.Sy jailops-backupd .
.Bl -tag -width jailops_backupd_config
.It Va jailops_backupd_enable
Set to
.Dq YES
to start the node at boot.
.It Va jailops_backupd_config
The configuration file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/backupd.yaml .
.It Va jailops_backupd_runas
The unprivileged user.
Default
.Sy jailops-backup .
.El
.Pp
The configuration is validated as that user with
.Dl service jailops_backupd checkconfig
and a start refuses a configuration that does not validate.
There is no
.Cm reload .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width JAILOPS_BACKUPD_CONFIG
.It Ev JAILOPS_BACKUPD_CONFIG
The configuration file when
.Fl c
is not given.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Stop: the listeners close, open sessions end and running jobs are cancelled.
.It Dv SIGHUP
Not handled: there is no reload, and the process ends as with any signal it
does not catch.
A change of the configuration needs a restart.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/backupd.yaml
The configuration; the installed sample is
.Pa backupd.yaml.sample .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/backupd.dsn
The database connection string, as the sample names it
.Pq Sy database.dsn_file ;
it must be readable by its owner only.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops-backupd.sock
The admin socket, mode 0600, root only
.Pq Sy admin_socket ;
the sample puts it at
.Pa /var/run/jailops-backupd/admin.sock .
.It Pa /var/run/jailops-backupd/backupd.pid
The pid of the daemon under rc.d.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/backupd.crt
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/backupd.key
The server certificate and key
.Pq Sy tls ;
the sample keeps them under
.Pa /var/db/jailops-backup .
.It Pa /var/db/jailops-backup/repository
The repository, with the directory datastore of the sample.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
The command failed: the configuration does not load, the daemon or the
database cannot be reached, a job failed, or a command was given a bad flag or
the wrong arguments.
.It 2
Usage: no command, an unknown command, or an unknown option before the
command.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jailops 1 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr jailopsd 8
.Pp
The backup and restore guide is part of the JailOps documentation.
